1
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,560
He might get away with it this time,
but if there's a next time,

2
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,360
he won't be so lucky.

3
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,800
Thanks for serving that up.

4
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,280
Now get ready for my return.

5
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Is there a chance</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Father will wake up soon?</font></font></i>

6
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,600
It's 50-50, Ms. Nada.

7
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,080
Please take good care of him, Doctor.

8
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:00,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You know my father's all I have left.</font></font></i>

9
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:03,680
I don't trust Phakorn at all.
So he's using the Tayawat name now, right?

10
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,440
-Yes.
-If that's all, I'll be going.

11
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,640
Okay, Wee.

12
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,560
-Call me what you did before.
-Okay, Wee.

13
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:13,000
With that Rawee going too,
I'm even more worried.

14
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:16,080
Why are you still so biased against Wee?

15
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,960
Wee?

16
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Once this is over,</font></font></i>

17
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I won't get involved with her anymore.</font></font></i>

18
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,240
You can stop worrying.

19
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:28,120
I'm sorry I punched you, Wee.

20
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,240
SUN SECRETS RESORT, TAWAN ISLAND

21
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:26,600
Ms. Nada.

22
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,200
-Hello, Ms. Nada.
-Hello.

23
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,800
Someone told me you were staying here.

24
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,000
Have you changed your mind?

25
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,360
I haven't thought about it yet.

26
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,360
Can we talk first?

27
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,480
I'm tired. I'd like to go inside and rest.

28
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,520
Sometimes I can't help wondering

29
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,080
if you're really Ms. Nada.

30
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,720
You're hot and cold.

31
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,840
I could blame it on the attack,

32
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:15,000
but you've been acting strangely
ever since we met abroad.

33
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,760
Ms. Nada.

34
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,440
You're Nada Tayawat, right?

35
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:49,320
I'm Jak, Nimit's younger brother.

36
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,800
You look even more handsome.
I barely recognized you.

37
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,800
Thank you.

38
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:01,400
You've changed too, Ms. Nada.
You're much prettier and more stylish now.

39
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,520
You talked to me like we were old friends.

40
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,800
But back in Thailand,

41
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:13,680
you wouldn't even give me a second glance.

42
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,600
You acted like you couldn't stand me.

43
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,120
And when we went out for dinner,

44
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,200
all you did was ask questions about Nimit,

45
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,480
your family, and yourself.

46
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,560
Do you still have my phone number?

47
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,280
Yes.

48
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,480
I secretly got it from Nimit's phone.

49
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:41,240
Let me see.
I'm not sure if it's my current number.

50
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,480
Here.

51
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,200
No, that's not my number anymore.

52
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:00,520
Then could I have your new number?

53
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,720
Sure.

54
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,320
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

55
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You deleted your old number from my phone</font></font></i>

56
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and saved your new one instead.</font></font></i>

57
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:22,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">And after that,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">you never answered my calls.</font></font></i>

58
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,760
How long will you
keep bringing up the past?

59
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,160
I don't have all day for you.

60
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,440
You ran away from me
and went back to Thailand.

61
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,840
You wouldn't answer my calls
or contact me.

62
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,560
Then I found you with that bastard Rawich.

63
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,320
And you looked at me with disgust again.

64
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,640
Tell me something.

65
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,960
When did you and that bastard
get together?

66
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,280
Hey!

67
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,000
Show some respect.

68
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,360
I don't remember
what you're talking about.

69
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,400
You're not going anywhere.

70
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,320
Let go of me, Mr. Jak! Let go!

71
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,640
Do you remember what happened?

72
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,200
There's something

73
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:04,200
that's been bothering me to this day.

74
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:07,640
Ms. Nada.

75
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,440
You haven't been answering my calls.

76
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:14,120
Did I do something to upset you?
Why are you avoiding me?

77
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,520
You've got the wrong person.

78
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:22,240
Ms. Nada! Ms. Nada, wait!

79
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,800
Wait a minute!

80
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:30,360
Oh, Jak.

81
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,400
Have you eaten yet?

82
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,880
I didn't notice it that day.

83
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,680
I was so annoyed that I forgot to ask

84
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,080
how you got to Nimit's house before me.

85
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,160
That was impossible.

86
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,880
And you were with that jerk.

87
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,680
But your clothes and hair were different.

88
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,120
When did you find time to change?

89
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:04,800
Let go.

90
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,680
I don't remember anything.

91
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,800
Hey.

92
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,720
But I let it go

93
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,840
because you started
being nice to me again,

94
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,720
and Rawich was already dead.

95
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:17,840
Are you finished?

96
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:20,560
I told you I don't remember anything.

97
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:23,240
You know I was attacked

98
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,400
and lost some of my memory.

99
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,720
You have a sister, don't you?

100
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,480
Are you out of your mind?

101
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,640
Ms. Nada! Come out and talk to me!

102
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:34,400
-Open the door! Ms. Nada!
-Thong!

103
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,520
-Open it right now!
-Thong!

104
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,080
-Thong!
-I said open the door!

105
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:38,520
Ms. Nada!

106
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,240
-Thong!
-Ms. Nada!

107
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,720
Ms. Nada!

108
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,520
Ms. Nada, who are you really?

109
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,360
You're not the real Nada, are you?

110
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,680
Ms. Nada!

111
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,520
Ms. Nada! Come out and talk to me!

112
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,520
Ms. Nada! Come out
and talk to me properly.

113
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:57,200
Or I'll have my men spread the word
that you're not the real Nada!

114
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,760
Ms. Nada!

115
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:13,120
Ms. Nada! Come out
and talk to me properly.

116
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,280
Ms. Nada!

117
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,840
Ms. Nada! I said, open the door!

118
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,880
-Ms. Nada! Hey!
-What are you doing?

119
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,560
What the hell?

120
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:40,960
You're trying to scare Ms. Nada

121
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:42,160
into selling you her house, right?

122
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:45,880
-What the hell are you talking about?
-Want to live to spend your money?

123
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,120
Yes!

124
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:52,560
Okay.

125
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,120
I give up.

126
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,400
Don't let me catch you
anywhere near Ms. Nada again.

127
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,400
Get lost!

128
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:15,920
Thamrong.

129
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:22,160
Don't be scared. You're safe now.

130
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,320
You're safe now.

131
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,040
Get some more rest.

132
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,000
I'm fine now.

133
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,720
I'm sorry about Thong.

134
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,720
He probably thought you were a thief.

135
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,840
Does that man work here?

136
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:12,120
Yes.

137
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:14,440
He looks after the house when I'm away.

138
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,200
What brings you here, Ms. Nada?

139
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,640
Someone wants to buy this house.

140
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:27,320
The same person
who's buying Mr. Nimit's resort.

141
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,280
Ms. Nada, earlier…

142
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:36,480
Now that you're awake,
why not go back and rest at the resort?

143
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:38,680
The people there
must be worried about you.

144
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,040
Okay.

145
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,880
Thank you very much.

146
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,520
Goodbye.

147
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,760
Don't be scared. You're safe now.

148
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,160
You're safe now.

149
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,560
Wee, have you seen Uncle Thamrong?

150
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:30,000
We were talking when he got a call
and rushed off.

151
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:32,800
I don't know where he went.
Alyssa's worried about him.

152
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,800
I haven't seen him around here.

153
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,560
What about you? Where have you been?

154
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:43,480
I went for a walk.

155
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,920
I ran into Ms. Nada, too.

156
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,520
I didn't know she was here.

157
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:50,000
Did she tell you she was coming?

158
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,600
Is that kid gone?

159
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:07,800
-Thong.
-What is it?

160
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,640
Don't hurt Rawee again.

161
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,320
Don't go soft on him.

162
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:17,480
Have you forgotten what they did to us?

163
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,920
But Rawee

164
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,280
is my own nephew, after all.

165
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,960
But he saw you with Thamrong.

166
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:33,480
Never mind.
Rawee probably won't tell anyone.

167
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,560
He has nothing to do with this.

168
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,560
Please, I'm begging you.

169
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:39,840
Don't hurt Rawee again.

170
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,640
If they find out the whole truth

171
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,600
about everything we've done,

172
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:47,720
do you think they'll forgive us?

173
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,360
He's only nice to you

174
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,080
because he thinks you're Nada,

175
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,200
not Lada.

176
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,520
Oh.

177
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:10,200
I've found Uncle Thamrong.

178
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:12,520
Did he say where he'd been?

179
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,240
He said he had urgent business nearby.

180
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,160
What about you, Mr. Rawee?

181
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,640
I went for a walk on the beach.

182
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,640
I ran into Ms. Nada too.

183
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,720
Oh.

184
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:31,000
Aunt Da's here too?
She didn't tell me she was coming.

185
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,960
Let's go get ready for dinner.

186
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,720
Uncle Thamrong, Aunt Da is on the island.

187
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,520
I called her, but she didn't answer.

188
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,680
Could you invite her to dinner?

189
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,120
-Of course.
-Thank you.

190
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,760
I'll wait at the restaurant.

191
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:02,720
Okay.

192
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,400
Uncle.

193
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,520
Did you already know Ms. Nada was here?

194
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,760
You don't seem surprised at all.

195
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,760
Well, Ms. Nada has a vacation house here.

196
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,640
It's not strange for her to visit.

197
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:25,400
But Mother didn't tell me either.
Should I come with you?

198
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,080
No, that's alright.

199
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:29,320
You two go freshen up.

200
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:32,000
I'll go get her myself, okay?
See you at the restaurant.

201
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,080
Is something wrong, Wee?

202
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,800
You've been giving
Uncle Thamrong strange looks.

203
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:57,280
I'm just wondering how close

204
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:58,800
Ms. Nada and Uncle Thamrong are.

205
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,920
They're not that close.

206
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,680
They mostly know each other
through Uncle Nimit.

207
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:09,600
Why? Did you find something out?

208
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:14,360
He was partly trying to intimidate me
into selling him the house.

209
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,440
But I think

210
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:20,040
Jak has suspected for a long time

211
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:22,400
that I'm not the real Nada.

212
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,880
Even if he goes around telling people,
no one will believe him.

213
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:30,560
You and Ms. Nada look almost identical.

214
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,960
Hello?

215
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,720
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Is this Nada Tayawat?</font></font></i>

216
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,240
Yes.

217
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,840
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I'm so glad.</font></font></i>

218
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,440
Who's this?

219
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,400
Lada.

220
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:11,720
Lada?

221
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:17,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You've forgotten all about me.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I guess I mean nothing to you now.</font></font></i>

222
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:20,920
And here I've been thinking

223
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,640
about you every day.

224
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:28,480
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Have you forgotten</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">your sister on Tawan Island?</font></font></i>

225
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,960
Lada? Is that really you?

226
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:37,400
Yes, it's me.

227
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:43,400
Living the good life
and forgetting all about me, huh?

228
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:46,920
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">It's not like that.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I've been trying to contact you all along.</font></font></i>

229
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,320
But I had to do it secretly.
I was afraid Father would find out.

230
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:54,240
I was afraid

231
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:57,480
you'd be torn away
from your family, just like I was.

232
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,760
I thought you were afraid

233
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,760
I'd take away your happiness.

234
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:06,840
That's not true.

235
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:10,920
I'm not as happy here as you think.

236
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:14,160
I feel like an outsider in this family,

237
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,600
someone nobody wants.

238
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:19,360
I've been trying to find a way
to leave this house.

239
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:27,240
Do you have a recent photo of yourself?

240
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:29,520
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Yes.</font></font></i>

241
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,920
Send me one, will you?

242
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,200
Sure.

243
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:38,520
But what do you need it for?

244
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:44,640
I just want to see
my little sister's face.

245
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,160
We haven't seen each other in 20 years.

246
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:51,840
I want to see how much

247
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,440
you've changed, Nada.

248
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,160
Okay, I'll send you one.

249
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:01,360
But where should I send it?

250
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:33,440
Then why is this bothering you again?

251
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:38,120
I feel guilty about those two boys.

252
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:41,320
Rawee deserves
better opportunities in life.

253
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:44,040
But everything we did
was to protect Rawee.

254
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,720
And Phakorn ended up paying the price.

255
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:53,640
He went from an innocent boy
to someone selfish.

256
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:56,880
Just because

257
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:00,280
I wanted revenge on the Tayawat family.

258
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,880
Don't blame yourself for everything.

259
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,160
Phakorn survived
because you got him treated.

260
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:13,000
He also got a good education
thanks to you.

261
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:15,680
Think about it.

262
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:18,680
If Rawee were in Phakorn's place,
he might've turned out differently.

263
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:21,840
I think it also depends

264
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,440
on their personalities.

265
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:33,840
Do you think

266
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:37,960
those two boys
will turn against each other?

267
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,240
If they do,

268
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:45,880
it won't be just because of you.

269
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:49,280
There could be other reasons too.

270
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:54,120
Don't overthink it.

271
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:55,920
Try to relax.

272
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:58,600
Come here.

273
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:12,800
You don't need to worry so much.

274
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:28,360
Have you ever thought

275
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:32,200
about what if Ms. Nada
isn't your real mother?

276
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:36,000
What do you mean?

277
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:40,440
Well, what if Ms. Nada is an impostor?

278
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,400
That's impossible.

279
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,080
If anyone were an impostor,

280
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:47,520
it'd be me.

281
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:50,800
Like, maybe I was switched
with another baby.

282
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:57,920
A DNA comparison between Nada and Rawee…

283
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:02,200
They're not mother and son.

284
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,200
How can Wee not be her son?

285
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,200
Wee, actually…

286
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,640
Stop worrying about this, Korn.

287
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:18,800
Didn't you already decide
to stay and repay Ms. Nada?

288
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:23,120
Wherever you're happy living,

289
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,840
I'm fine with it.

290
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,800
What if the truth comes out?

291
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,080
I'll take responsibility.

292
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:31,240
How can you take responsibility for that?

293
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:35,400
I'll take all the blame.
You don't have to worry.

294
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,200
Then where will I live?

295
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:39,480
Where you live now.

296
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:41,120
Ms. Nada's condo.

297
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:44,040
-As what?
-My younger brother.

298
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:46,040
As if everyone would accept that.

299
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:48,240
If they don't, we can find
somewhere else to live.

300
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,800
Why do you make everything sound so easy?

301
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:57,000
Why make things harder than they are?

302
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:59,240
I won't let you struggle, Korn.

303
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,200
We're brothers, no matter what.

304
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,440
Hearing you say that
just makes me feel even guiltier.

305
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,720
I've treated you badly so many times.

306
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,200
You even punched me.

307
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:16,680
I was jealous.

308
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:19,160
I've told you a hundred times, Korn.

309
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:21,560
I don't have feelings for Ms. Alyssa.

310
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:28,200
But Alyssa might have feelings for you.

311
00:26:29,120 --> 00:26:30,280
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You like me, don't you?</font></font></i>

312
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,720
You keep coming around
and using this as an excuse.

313
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:35,880
You did all this because you like me,
didn't you?

314
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:37,760
What if I said I do?

315
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:40,960
Then I'd tell you
I don't feel the same way.

316
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:45,080
That's ridiculous.

317
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:06,000
Who's joining us for dinner tonight?

318
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:07,360
I think everyone will be there.

319
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:09,560
Alyssa, Phakorn, and Rawee.

320
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:14,720
I'm going to put an end to all this soon.

321
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:18,520
I've been waiting to hear that.

322
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:21,640
It won't be long now.

323
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:24,160
I've got everything ready.

324
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,160
I'm just waiting for that old bastard
to wake up.

325
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:31,920
How's your father doing now?

326
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:37,120
He's getting exactly what he deserves.

327
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:40,360
He's in a coma.

328
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:42,680
His children are fighting.

329
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,960
And the fortune he built

330
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:48,760
is ending up in someone else's hands.

331
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:53,080
I think he's already suffered enough

332
00:27:53,600 --> 00:27:55,040
for what he did to you.

333
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:01,320
-Thamrong.
-Yes?

334
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:03,000
When all this is over,

335
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:06,440
will you move abroad with me?

336
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:16,240
Thank you, Doctor.

337
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,040
Is something wrong?

338
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:58,280
I was just discussing
Dad's treatment plan with the doctor.

339
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,680
How did it go?

340
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:10,280
It's pretty serious.

341
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:14,640
He needs surgery and chemotherapy.

342
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:18,960
I feel so sorry for him.

343
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:24,400
If he'd told me sooner, he could've gotten
treatment before things got worse.

344
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:29,280
Try looking at it another way.

345
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:32,760
Your father probably wanted to wait
for the right time.

346
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:37,360
He likely wanted to get everything
sorted out before telling you.

347
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,320
Are you Dad's lawyer now?

348
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:48,000
You're good at playing mediator.

349
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:53,560
Is it working?

350
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:20,920
I'll excuse myself.

351
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:45,920
Is something wrong?

352
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:49,600
Just a little something.

353
00:30:57,320 --> 00:30:58,680
Is it about your father?

354
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:08,200
You know, I think you and Wee
make a good match.

355
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:16,960
You seem happier with him
than you do with me.

356
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,600
Is there something you want to tell me?

357
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:25,280
Can you stop picking a fight?

358
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,520
I'm already upset.

359
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:31,800
But you seemed perfectly happy just now.

360
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:35,440
Mr. Rawee was asking about Dad.

361
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:39,560
If you won't ask about him,
at least don't pick a fight.

362
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:47,640
So because I don't care about your father
as much as Wee does,

363
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:49,120
you don't like me?

364
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,960
Listen, Alyssa.

365
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:57,400
We're dating now.
You could at least show me some respect.

366
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:01,760
How have I disrespected you?

367
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:07,800
You were smiling at my brother,
but you look annoyed when I show up.

368
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:11,080
Why, Alyssa?

369
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:13,560
Is being with me really that miserable?

370
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,920
Sometimes I wonder

371
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,720
if you kept rejecting me

372
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,160
because you already had feelings
for someone else.

373
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:27,720
And knowing you and Wee
have a history together

374
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:31,600
just makes me even more certain.
It's Wee you have feelings for, isn't it?

375
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:37,760
Are you trying to start a fight?

376
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:40,920
I'm just asking.

377
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:43,440
Have you ever asked yourself

378
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,640
if you're sincere about anything?

379
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:47,680
What do you mean?

380
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:51,760
Is there something you want to tell me?

381
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:54,440
I've told you everything.

382
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:58,240
Except for the results of your DNA test
with Aunt Da.

383
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:01,680
What are you talking about?

384
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:04,160
The truth you're too afraid to admit.

385
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:07,880
That you're not Aunt Da's biological son.

386
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:11,800
Where did you get that idea?

387
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:17,120
From the DNA test Ms. Pimpa
secretly had done on you and Aunt Da.

388
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:20,400
You know about that?

389
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:23,360
Yes.

390
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,120
And I've been waiting for you
to tell everyone.

391
00:33:27,320 --> 00:33:29,960
How long will you keep posing
as Aunt Da's son?

392
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:37,120
Then who do you think her real son is?

393
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:38,600
Wee?

394
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:40,920
Let me tell you something.

395
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,360
Neither Wee nor I

396
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,040
is Ms. Nada's son.

397
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:50,160
Ms. Pimpa didn't just have
my blood and Ms. Nada's tested.

398
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:52,160
She had Wee's blood tested too.

399
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:55,800
And the results confirmed
that neither of us

400
00:33:56,440 --> 00:33:58,520
is Ms. Nada's son.

401
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:02,280
GENETIC ASSURANCE SYSTEMS

402
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:04,480
Please make sure she gets them.

403
00:34:05,760 --> 00:34:06,680
Of course.

404
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:37,639
I don't care

405
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:40,600
who Aunt Da's biological son is.

406
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:44,120
I just want you to know

407
00:34:44,199 --> 00:34:46,120
you've been dishonest with me
from the start.

408
00:34:48,239 --> 00:34:49,520
Remember that hat?

409
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:52,639
It wasn't even yours.

410
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:56,199
It belonged to your brother.
You just never told me.

411
00:34:58,080 --> 00:35:00,040
And the Tayawat surname,

412
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:04,600
that isn't really yours either.

413
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:13,800
Don't worry.

414
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:16,120
I won't tell anyone.

415
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:20,920
You got yourself into this mess,
so fix it.

416
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:24,360
But as a friend, I just want to warn you.

417
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:28,800
Don't let this go any further.

418
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:02,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Don't worry.</font></font></i>

419
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:04,600
I won't tell anyone.

420
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:08,920
You got yourself into this mess,
so fix it.

421
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:12,760
But as a friend, I just want to warn you.

422
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:17,240
Don't let this go any further.

423
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:35,520
Have some shrimp.

424
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:40,480
-Your coconut water.
-Thank you.

425
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:51,760
Did you two have a fight?

426
00:36:57,360 --> 00:37:00,120
No. Mom, you probably don't know yet,

427
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:03,760
but Alyssa and I
are officially dating now.

428
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,400
I just told Mr. Nimit we're dating.

429
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:15,480
But you and Uncle Thamrong
seem much closer than I realized.

430
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:20,600
Well, we met through Mr. Nimit.
We've seen each other quite often.

431
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:22,200
We've helped each other out a few times.

432
00:37:23,920 --> 00:37:24,920
Helped each other?

433
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:29,640
Yes. Sometimes I can't finish everything,
so I ask Thamrong to help.

434
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:50,760
Having dinner without inviting me?

435
00:37:54,720 --> 00:37:59,000
We didn't invite you
because we don't want you at our table.

436
00:38:00,200 --> 00:38:01,600
Why is that so hard to understand?

437
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,000
Oh.

438
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:08,600
I thought someone

439
00:38:08,680 --> 00:38:11,560
might be afraid I'd spill a secret.

440
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:19,640
Say whatever you want.

441
00:38:23,200 --> 00:38:25,960
Why don't you join us for dinner?

442
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:28,440
We can celebrate your big win, Mr. Jak.

443
00:38:29,160 --> 00:38:33,200
Congratulations on taking
your niece's resort.

444
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:44,040
No, thanks.

445
00:38:44,640 --> 00:38:46,800
I just stopped by to say hello.

446
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,520
Enjoy your dinner.

447
00:38:50,200 --> 00:38:54,400
It's on me. I'll be going now.

448
00:39:07,640 --> 00:39:10,240
Mom, did you have a fight with Uncle Jak?

449
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:12,680
Why was he talking like that?

450
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:17,280
It's nothing. He's always
running his mouth like that.

451
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:22,080
Come to think of it, you've been there
for Ms. Nada through it all too.

452
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:25,840
What do you mean, Wee?

453
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:31,400
Nothing. Just making conversation.
Don't read too much into it.

454
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:46,480
Oh, Alyssa. Are you full already?

455
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:49,400
Yes.

456
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:52,640
I'm feeling a little tired.

457
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:58,120
Sorry, Aunt Da. I arranged this dinner,
but would you mind if I left early?

458
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:02,400
Not at all. We can have dinner again
when we're back in Bangkok.

459
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:03,320
Go get some rest.

460
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:08,200
I'll take you back.

461
00:40:18,520 --> 00:40:20,800
Then I'll excuse myself too.

462
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:23,160
I have to get up early tomorrow,
so I'd better get some rest.

463
00:40:24,760 --> 00:40:25,720
Alright.

464
00:40:32,520 --> 00:40:35,840
I think they're definitely suspicious
of something.

465
00:40:37,480 --> 00:40:40,120
Don't worry. I'll keep an eye on things.

466
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:45,520
But where is your brother right now?

467
00:41:33,280 --> 00:41:34,560
Don't worry.

468
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:37,080
I won't tell anyone.

469
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:41,640
You got yourself into this mess,
so fix it.

470
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:45,160
But as a friend, I just want to warn you.

471
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,480
Don't let this go any further.

472
00:42:09,520 --> 00:42:10,560
Wee.

473
00:42:12,080 --> 00:42:13,680
Yeah? What is it?

474
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:29,000
Alyssa knows I'm not Ms. Nada's son.

475
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:42,000
She secretly looked
at Ms. Pimpa's DNA test results, right?

476
00:42:44,160 --> 00:42:46,200
-You knew?
-Yes.

477
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:49,440
Then why didn't you tell me?

478
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:54,800
Listen, Korn.

479
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:57,560
If she decides whether to date you

480
00:42:57,640 --> 00:42:59,320
based on whether you're a Tayawat,

481
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:03,200
then she's probably not worth dating.

482
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:08,400
But the point is, I lied to her, Wee.

483
00:43:10,080 --> 00:43:11,800
It's not something you could tell her.

484
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:14,680
So what are you going to do?

485
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:17,760
Is that why you two fought?

486
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:26,400
I don't know yet.
I haven't figured it out.

487
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:31,640
Earlier, you asked

488
00:43:32,840 --> 00:43:34,920
what if Ms. Nada wasn't my mother?

489
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:36,880
Why did you ask that?

490
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:40,320
Did you find something out?

491
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:56,920
Today, I saw Ms. Nada with Uncle Thamrong.

492
00:43:58,920 --> 00:44:01,080
Before that, I saw Mr. Jak

493
00:44:01,160 --> 00:44:02,560
talking to Ms. Nada.

494
00:44:04,240 --> 00:44:05,760
They seemed to be arguing.

495
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:09,520
Then Uncle Thamrong
stepped in to help her.

496
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:14,800
I wouldn't have thought
anything was strange

497
00:44:16,840 --> 00:44:18,160
if I hadn't seen them hugging.

498
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:20,760
Hugging?

499
00:44:23,760 --> 00:44:25,400
Remember what I told you?

500
00:44:26,840 --> 00:44:30,320
Ms. Nada's handwriting didn't match
the handwriting in the diary.

501
00:44:33,480 --> 00:44:34,520
I WANT A LITTLE CAFE OF MY OWN

502
00:44:34,600 --> 00:44:35,720
DECORATED JUST THE WAY I LIKE IT

503
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:36,800
PROJECT OVERVIEW BEFORE THE BOARD MEETING

504
00:44:36,880 --> 00:44:37,880
NEW PROJECT DESIGNS, CANCEL THE MEETING

505
00:44:38,640 --> 00:44:41,520
The handwriting doesn't match.
Like two different people wrote them.

506
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:51,360
If Wee is her real son,

507
00:44:53,320 --> 00:44:54,640
who is this woman?

508
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:00,560
I remember.

509
00:45:02,280 --> 00:45:03,600
That's why I'm asking you.

510
00:45:04,160 --> 00:45:06,960
Why did you ask
what if Ms. Nada wasn't my mother?

511
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:11,880
Do you know something I don't?

512
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:17,760
Actually…

513
00:45:21,560 --> 00:45:23,320
Where the hell are you taking me?

514
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:26,160
Shut the hell up. Now get moving.

515
00:45:26,240 --> 00:45:27,320
Go!

516
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:41,280
What do you want?
You want money, don't you?

517
00:45:41,360 --> 00:45:43,040
Shut up and keep walking.

518
00:45:49,720 --> 00:45:50,920
Where are you taking me?

519
00:45:59,400 --> 00:46:01,160
Help!

520
00:46:02,560 --> 00:46:03,600
Somebody help!

521
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:06,800
What's all the screaming for?

522
00:46:11,880 --> 00:46:14,760
You know too much. You deserve to die.

523
00:46:15,520 --> 00:46:17,200
Don't! Don't shoot.

524
00:46:18,400 --> 00:46:21,080
I'm scared. I swear.

525
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:22,480
I won't say a word.

526
00:46:22,560 --> 00:46:24,320
I'll keep everything a secret.

527
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:26,160
I'll never bring up the past again.

528
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:34,640
Don't shoot!

529
00:47:07,800 --> 00:47:09,200
You! Come here!

530
00:47:30,200 --> 00:47:31,280
Wee!

531
00:47:39,760 --> 00:47:42,360
Korn, hurry and pull me up.

532
00:47:45,200 --> 00:47:46,800
If both parents have passed away,

533
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:50,480
can a DNA test
still be done using other relatives?

534
00:47:51,400 --> 00:47:54,760
Like the maternal grandfather
or grandmother?

535
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:58,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Yes. We can test DNA</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">using the maternal grandparents</font></font></i>

536
00:47:59,040 --> 00:48:00,480
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">because a grandchild</font></font></i>

537
00:48:00,560 --> 00:48:04,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">shares about 25%</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">of their DNA with each one.</font></font></i>

538
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:06,480
So that means

539
00:48:07,320 --> 00:48:10,520
if either grandparent has passed away,

540
00:48:11,440 --> 00:48:13,880
the results won't be accurate, right?

541
00:48:13,960 --> 00:48:18,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">That's right.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But there are other ways we can test,</font></font></i>

542
00:48:18,240 --> 00:48:20,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">such as through the paternal grandparents.</font></font></i>

543
00:48:23,160 --> 00:48:25,040
-Let me see that.
-Wee!

544
00:48:25,120 --> 00:48:26,560
-That's mine. Don't touch it.
-Wait.

545
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:29,120
Wait, Korn. Let me see it first.

546
00:48:29,720 --> 00:48:31,360
-No. Don't touch it.
-Wait, Korn.

547
00:48:52,760 --> 00:48:55,640
Mom! Something's wrong with Korn!

548
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:21,400
You keep pretending
you're on my side, Wee.

549
00:49:21,480 --> 00:49:23,680
But you're out to stab me in the back,
aren't you?

550
00:49:25,840 --> 00:49:29,200
Or are you jealous
that I have a better life?

551
00:49:41,800 --> 00:49:45,840
Korn, hurry and pull me up!
I can't hold on much longer.

552
00:49:58,040 --> 00:50:01,720
This is Wee, Rawee.
He's your older brother.

553
00:50:01,800 --> 00:50:04,080
We grew up together.

554
00:50:04,160 --> 00:50:07,800
He's both your friend and your brother.
He's someone

555
00:50:07,880 --> 00:50:09,520
you love more than anyone.

556
00:50:09,600 --> 00:50:11,160
You're healthy now.

557
00:50:11,240 --> 00:50:14,120
You graduated overseas. You've gained
so much already. What more do you want?

558
00:50:14,200 --> 00:50:16,520
I've come too far, Wee. I can't go back…

559
00:50:17,480 --> 00:50:19,840
Or do you want your position
as the son back?

560
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:24,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you're watching this video,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">you have to remember him.</font></font></i>

561
00:50:25,200 --> 00:50:27,360
Don't ever forget him.

562
00:50:27,440 --> 00:50:31,520
Because the man beside you
is the person who loves you the most.

563
00:50:31,600 --> 00:50:35,360
He'll always help you,
support you in everything you do,

564
00:50:35,440 --> 00:50:37,160
and you can trust him.

565
00:51:26,640 --> 00:51:29,040
-Is something wrong?
-Someone called

566
00:51:29,120 --> 00:51:30,440
about two guests who came with you.

567
00:51:30,520 --> 00:51:33,040
One fell off a cliff,
and the other was shot.

568
00:51:34,960 --> 00:51:38,200
-Where are they now?
-At the viewpoint behind the resort.

569
00:51:44,760 --> 00:51:46,960
Uncle!

570
00:51:47,680 --> 00:51:48,840
Uncle!

571
00:51:53,520 --> 00:51:57,480
ALYSSA

572
00:52:03,720 --> 00:52:04,960
Excuse me.

573
00:52:11,640 --> 00:52:12,840
Hello, Ms. Alyssa.

574
00:52:15,360 --> 00:52:17,840
Oh, I just stepped out for a walk.

575
00:52:20,080 --> 00:52:23,800
Yes, of course. I'll be right there.
Wait at the resort. Don't come here.

576
00:52:23,880 --> 00:52:25,560
Okay, I'll keep you updated.

577
00:52:28,440 --> 00:52:29,680
What is it?

578
00:52:40,600 --> 00:52:44,360
I overheard the staff talking.
One fell off a cliff. The other was shot.

579
00:52:45,360 --> 00:52:48,120
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Who fell off the cliff? Was it Phakorn?</font></font></i>

580
00:52:48,960 --> 00:52:50,040
No, sir.

581
00:52:50,120 --> 00:52:53,840
Mr. Phakorn is still alive,
but I'm not sure if he was shot.

582
00:52:53,920 --> 00:52:55,000
He was taken to the local clinic.

583
00:52:56,200 --> 00:52:58,840
And that bitch Da? Have you found her yet?

584
00:52:59,720 --> 00:53:00,880
Yes, sir.

585
00:53:00,960 --> 00:53:04,280
She's been with some man the whole time.
I haven't been able to get near her.

586
00:53:06,200 --> 00:53:07,120
Who the hell is he?

587
00:53:08,360 --> 00:53:11,240
Well, if you get a chance,

588
00:53:11,960 --> 00:53:13,480
finish her off.

589
00:53:14,120 --> 00:53:15,800
Don't screw it up like last time.

590
00:53:16,400 --> 00:53:17,360
Yes, sir.

591
00:53:21,560 --> 00:53:24,240
Hey, Off. I wonder if they'll find him.

592
00:53:24,320 --> 00:53:26,600
He fell off a cliff, not a chair.

593
00:53:26,680 --> 00:53:29,200
It was so deep. I doubt he survived.

594
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:31,800
Poor Mr. Rawee.

595
00:53:31,880 --> 00:53:33,360
I hope they find him.

596
00:53:33,440 --> 00:53:34,440
Yeah.

597
00:53:39,200 --> 00:53:42,000
Wee, I'm warning you.

598
00:53:42,720 --> 00:53:44,520
Stay away from Ms. Nada.

599
00:54:11,560 --> 00:54:13,440
Tell Phakorn to stay where he is.
I'm on my way.

600
00:54:13,520 --> 00:54:14,480
Okay.

601
00:54:15,520 --> 00:54:16,680
Phakorn.

602
00:54:17,800 --> 00:54:19,000
Stay right there.

603
00:54:20,400 --> 00:54:23,840
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Mr. Thamrong is coming to help.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Don't go anywhere.</font></font></i>

604
00:54:26,320 --> 00:54:29,160
Wee said his name is Thong.

605
00:54:29,920 --> 00:54:31,320
He works at your house.

606
00:54:33,480 --> 00:54:37,840
I saw Thong holding Mr. Jak at gunpoint
and leading him away.

607
00:54:38,600 --> 00:54:40,120
So we followed them.

608
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:45,880
Then we saw Thong shoot Mr. Jak,
and he fell off the cliff.

609
00:54:48,600 --> 00:54:50,880
What about Rawee?

610
00:54:52,680 --> 00:54:53,880
Where is Rawee?

611
00:54:57,040 --> 00:54:58,760
He stepped in to help Mr. Jak.

612
00:55:01,600 --> 00:55:02,960
What's wrong?

613
00:55:06,480 --> 00:55:08,200
Why are you crying, Phakorn?

614
00:55:12,200 --> 00:55:14,000
But Thong attacked him.

615
00:55:16,520 --> 00:55:18,200
He fell off the cliff too.

616
00:55:34,200 --> 00:55:36,080
I couldn't save Wee in time.

617
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:21,400
They've found the body.

618
00:57:32,640 --> 00:57:35,680
I could understand if he was angry at Jak
for threatening me.

619
00:57:35,760 --> 00:57:38,920
But Rawee? Thong knows Rawee

620
00:57:39,000 --> 00:57:40,360
is Nada's son.

621
00:57:40,960 --> 00:57:42,160
Maybe it was an accident.

622
00:57:42,240 --> 00:57:44,520
Or maybe Thong wasn't the one who did it.

623
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:50,920
You can head back, Uncle.

624
00:57:52,120 --> 00:57:54,720
I want to stay
and wait for news about Wee.

625
00:57:57,400 --> 00:57:58,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I think</font></font></i>

626
00:57:59,880 --> 00:58:02,440
it's time you told the truth, Uncle.

627
00:58:08,680 --> 00:58:10,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Please be okay, Wee.</font></font></i>
